On 8/11/07, Daniel Goetzmann <cestricu@googlemail.com> wrote:
> To be honest, when I saw a fu'ivla starting in a vowel for the first time I
> didn't believe that it was a valid fu'ivla. But now I'm pretty sure that
> fu'ivla may start with a vowel under certain circumstances.

I don't know why the creator (Pierre) left the beginning vowel in
{agbakata}. Appart from that it looks fine as a stage 3 fu'ivla: it
has consonant clusters in the first five letters and ends in a vowel.
Jorge too seems to have agreed with such an unusual convention e.g.
{alba'aka}. I'd like to know why.

